 "tr_note": "The Textus Receptus adds αὐτὸς, 'himself', and, at the end, ἐν τῷ φανερῷ, 'in the open'. That is why the KJV reads 'himself shall reward thee openly', with the Geneva's 'openly' and the YLT's 'Himself ... manifestly'; the DRC, ASV and BSB have neither."
